# Export-ignore: what `git archive` leaves out of a release.
#
# The dev diary stays in tree and history (no delete, no rewrite) and is left
# out of the public tree, which is built fresh from `git archive`. This list
# carries only the paths that exist here.
#
# Why two openspec lines. gitattributes documents that a pattern matching a
# directory does not match the paths inside it, so `/openspec/**` is the
# contract: it sets export-ignore on every file (`git check-attr` per file).
# Alone it leaves an empty `openspec/` entry in the archive (measured, git
# 2.56), so `/openspec` prunes that directory entry too. Every line is anchored
# with a leading `/`, so no nested openspec or CLAUDE.md is caught.

# The dev diary (openspec/RATIFICATION.md goes with it).
/openspec      export-ignore
/openspec/**   export-ignore
# The plugin-root CLAUDE.md (.claude-plugin/ sits at the repo root).
/CLAUDE.md     export-ignore
